{"title":"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A set S consists of triangles whose sides have integer lengths less than 5, and no two elements of S are congruent or similar. What is the largest number of elements that S can have? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/567797ed33be3423790ac3b609dc91fe47ec8da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 9\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 10\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 11\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"376\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to be the set of all integral triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80414f2f94f70731e91b6e12c4e6934c8fa65de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca80e390c2eee07b24d2edc6023def9310a3c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ge b \\ge c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff759e1c84f47ce7e17f9124a8d420fb6afec69e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+c &gt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc75abe3727f853cd2bca2f352c1e9b2c6b4c5dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />. Now we enumerate the elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2118bc58f41746389def78ee659abf720bd1677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 4, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/8/e58cbef51c0b84b10a3cbc99bae0ab1897aff20e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 4, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e97a72de1a41e6ab97eac5cef3f05b12ef3ec38c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 4, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/6/5964ef53ef5b2718c2f2818ded2fca51a9bfacc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 4, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa911dcfdaf1d7c8d161016c2cab54eeca9a905e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 3, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f458f038467e2b9026fdb2b97926b566a9745a38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 3, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/37937cd013627c14944d14a1f4f669168c874be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 3, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e804b07a6641177cd5bf44a4d7af79b1192d509e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 3, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/d/45de0fb4f26ea0202268618243d20f72d8263949.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 3, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4a2c54eda84ebad3e26f2070294e034cc4537bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 2, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/4/3c4d0f837e9eaf6483102a55535bcc746d3ac3f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 2, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/26388c3ec54e044b5d4001c111e91dd33be2c071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 2, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e61637ce2d59296380ccb6f26edee8d45c60850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>It should be clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11ceba9d7455309f60178fe82bb6e81e6c01fa83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc73f3216cbfb7ceb707c9c143823d7e5e49f659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|T|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> minus the larger \"duplicates\" (e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/4/3c4d0f837e9eaf6483102a55535bcc746d3ac3f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 2, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> is a larger duplicate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e61637ce2d59296380ccb6f26edee8d45c60850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />). Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc73f3216cbfb7ceb707c9c143823d7e5e49f659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|T|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the number of higher duplicates is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378a09b380bdddc44bd948b6bb68aed548e0bf66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/629ecb8ecd5f7e0c0f84efe07c0332d2647f54d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First of all, we can have at most one equilateral triangle in our set because all equilateral triangles are similar. We may pick the one with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35d43e6e252922c8df825114d48e1418c7516d6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThe isosceles non-equilateral triangles are composed of:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/4/f04f6498a9c3e3bc24eb3042cd9ad5f1f54da34b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2,2),(1,3,3),(1,4,4),(2,3,3),(2,4,4),(3,2,2),(3,4,4),(4,3,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"519\" height=\"20\" /> (ordered by base length)\n</p><p><br />\nThe triplets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/f/c1fb4be1e35424813a7838d9e5fba96a592074f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,1,1),(3,1,1),(4,1,1),(4,2,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"256\" height=\"20\" /> are not capable of forming triangles.\n</p><p><br />\nWe can include at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> isosceles non-equilateral triangles in our set. If we include all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f6451c56971edb3106b28f513ebf12afc9f1d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/7468a06b389fe08529fdf9f9ad0550374d3c238c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,4,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> will be similar.\n</p><p><br />\nFinally, there exists only one scalene triangle —— <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16bb9e5ba95f72b49640fcc7856f2e1c3ae664c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,3,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. This is the only such triangle because a triangle cannot be formed if we use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as the shortest side.\n</p><p><br />\nA triangle of one type will never clash with a triangle of another type under this categorization.\n</p><p><br />\nThe answer to the problem is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/5/6a5fa42ba48352188c4eefc455a148f166d6c401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+7+1=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~G2JFForever\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B\">2014 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2014 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017233905\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 292/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7092/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.260      1 -total\n 58.66%    7.778      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 39.13%    5.189      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12439:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017233905 and revision id 283737. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}